cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Computational studies toward multiphysics ultrasound
message: If you use this software or its results, please cite it.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-14
repository-code: "https://github.com/tue-bmd/multiphysics-ultrasound-models"
license: BSD-3-Clause
abstract: >-
  Four v0 simulation studies of multiphysics ultrasound modeling: vascular
  organization and its effects on mechanical relaxation and contrast transport,
  parameter identifiability from idealized mechanical and transport fields, and
  information transfer through a shared measurement operator, and reduction of
  vascular-matrix confounding through a calibrated SWE-CEUS relationship.
keywords:
  - quantitative ultrasound
  - inverse problems
  - identifiability
  - uncertainty quantification
  - contrast-enhanced ultrasound
  - shear wave elastography
authors:
  - family-names: Turco
    given-names: Simona
    email: s.turco@tue.nl
    affiliation: Eindhoven University of Technology
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1520-3930"
